    "diagnosis": "Solid pseudopillary neoplasm of the pancreas",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "There is a solid pseudopapillary neoplasm at the left of the image, which should be associated with a favorable outcome.&nbsp; The tumor cells have grooved nuclei and there are plentiful hyaline globules.&nbsp; Unfortunately for the patient, there is also an epithelioid angiosarcoma at the right of the slide, which appears overtly malignant.",
